This repository holds four packages, under two licenses. Each package directory
carries the license that applies to it, and that file governs its contents.

  PureQPBase/   MIT           See PureQPBase/LICENSE
  PureIPM/      MIT           See PureIPM/LICENSE
  PureDAQP/     MIT           See PureDAQP/LICENSE
  PureOSQP/     Apache-2.0    See PureOSQP/LICENSE

Everything outside those four directories -- the shared benchmarks, the
documentation, the design notes -- is MIT, on the terms in PureQPBase/LICENSE.

Why they differ:

PureOSQP is a derivative of OSQP (https://github.com/osqp/osqp), which is
distributed under the Apache License 2.0 and is copyright the OSQP authors. A
derivative carries its parent's terms, so PureOSQP is Apache-2.0 and cannot be
anything else.

PureQPBase and PureIPM are not derivatives of it. They were written from
published papers -- Ruiz 2001 for the equilibration, Banjac et al. 2019 for the
infeasibility certificates, Mehrotra 1992 for the interior-point method -- and
are released under the MIT license.

PureDAQP follows Arnstrom, Bemporad and Axehill 2022, and its authors' reference
C implementation (https://github.com/darnstrom/daqp) was read alongside the
paper. That implementation is MIT and copyright (c) 2022 Daniel Arnstrom; the
notice is retained in PureDAQP/LICENSE.

Depending on PureQPBase does not place a package under the MIT license, and
PureOSQP depending on it does not place PureQPBase under Apache-2.0.

See docs/src/attribution.md for what each package derives from, and the papers
to cite.

Copyright 2026 el-oso
